        </div>
        <div style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);font-size:0.84rem;font-style:italic;max-width:480px;">"Fantastic service, less than two hours after phoning up the job was done. The young man who fitted it was a credit to himself. I would highly recommend this company." John Manley</div>
        <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=Liverpool+Emergency+Plumber+reviews" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="background:#f97316;color:#ffffff;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;border:none;padding:0.4rem 1rem;border-radius:999px;">See our Google reviews →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUR APPROACH -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Our Approach to Bathroom Fitting in Liverpool</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We believe a bathroom should be a room you love using. Three rules guide every job we do.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>1. Premium materials only</strong><p>We fit Villeroy & Boch, Duravit, Geberit and Hansgrohe as standard. Tiles come from top UK and Italian suppliers. We pick brassware that holds its finish for years. The cheap chrome-plated zinc taps yellow in two years. We do not fit those.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>2. One team for everything</strong><p>Our team handles it all from start to finish. Plumbing and electrical work. Tiling and fitting. No subcontractors and no day-rate labour. The Gas Safe engineer plumbing your bathroom on Monday is the same person checking the tile work on Wednesday. You get one schedule, one point of contact and one written quote.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>3. Timeless over trendy</strong><p>We help you balance current design with materials that age well. Some 2026 trends are worth chasing. Microcement, freestanding baths and mixed-metal finishes will still look right in ten years. Others are short fads we steer you away from. The best bathrooms feel current the day they are finished and still feel right a decade later.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>4. Liverpool property fit</strong><p>Liverpool has Victorian terraces, 1930s semis and modern flats. We have fitted bathrooms in all of them. Each has its own quirks. Solid brick walls. Narrow footprints. Old soil stack positions. We plan the fit around the property at the free survey.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PREMIUM BRANDS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Premium Brands We Install in Liverpool Bathrooms</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We work with UK and EU premium makers. The names below are not aspirations. They are our standard spec.</p>

      <div class="pf-why-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Villeroy & Boch</h3>
          <p>German premium ceramics. The Subway range suits Liverpool bathrooms of any size. The glaze fights hard water build-up far better than cheap brands. That counts a lot in Merseyside.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Duravit</h3>
          <p>German design with clean modern lines. The Starck and ME by Starck ranges work in modern Liverpool flats. Strong warranties and spare parts on hand for decades.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Geberit</h3>
          <p>The Swiss top name for hidden cisterns and wall-hung toilet frames. We use the Geberit Duofix frame on every wall-hung fit. Their AquaClean shower toilet is now a common pick in our master en suites.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Hansgrohe</h3>
          <p>Top German shower brand. The AXOR and Raindance lines give real power and a feel that earns the price. The chrome and brass holds its colour for years. We pick Hansgrohe when shower quality matters most.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Grohe</h3>
          <p>The reliable name in premium taps. Strong UK stock of spare parts and steady quality across the range. We pick Grohe basin and bath taps when the look should feel quiet and well made.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Crosswater</h3>
          <p>A UK premium designer. Strong on modern brassware in non-chrome looks. Brushed brass, matte black and gunmetal for bathrooms that want more than chrome.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>Lusso Stone</h3>
          <p>A UK luxury brand. Solid stone basins, freestanding baths and bold vanities. Built for master bathrooms in Liverpool. Higher spec means longer lead times. But nothing else looks the same.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-why-item">
          <h3>BC Designs</h3>
          <p>A UK maker of premium freestanding baths and basins. Their copper and cast iron baths fit right at home in Liverpool's Victorian houses. These are big pieces meant to be the focal point.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-alert" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <strong>Why we don't fit budget brands</strong>
        <p>The bathroom market is full of cheap products that look the same on a shelf but break down in 2 to 5 years. Chrome plating peels. Cartridges fail. Tiles craze and stain. Swapping out cheap taps after 3 years costs as much as fitting top-end taps from day one. And you live with poor performance for the whole time. We only fit brands with a real long-term track record.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2026 TRENDS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>2026 Bathroom Trends in Liverpool Homes</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">These are the design trends shaping high-end bathrooms in 2026. Some will age well. Others are a calculated bet. We help you tell them apart at the free survey.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Microcement coatings</strong><p>Hand-applied thin cement coat across walls and floors. No grout lines. The look of polished concrete without the building work. Looks striking in modern Liverpool apartments. Needs a skilled hand to apply.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Sculptural freestanding baths</strong><p>The freestanding bath is back as the focal point of the room. Stone resin, copper finish and cast iron in clean modern shapes. We fit BC Designs and Lusso Stone where the bath is the centre piece. Best placed under a window or in the middle of larger Liverpool master bathrooms.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Curbless walk-in showers</strong><p>The 2026 shower has no tray and no door. The floor tile runs from dry zone to wet zone with a linear drain. Looks open. Easier to clean. Better for older or less mobile users. The fit needs full tanking and a precise floor fall, so most fitters will not quote them right.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Bold patterned wallpaper</strong><p>Bathroom wallpaper is back. The 2026 look is bold and patterned. Big flower prints on one feature wall above tiled lower halves. Looks great in Liverpool Victorian rooms. The bold pattern picks up on the old cornice work.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Statement lighting</strong><p>Pendants and lanterns are moving from living rooms into bathrooms. The look softens the hard edges of tile and stone. The light spec must be right for bathroom zones. We handle the IP-rated wiring as part of the job.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Hand-painted artisan tiles</strong><p>Mass-made graphic tiles are giving way to hand-painted Delft, soft floral and brush-stroke styles. Best in small Liverpool en suites and cloakrooms. One wall can be a feature without taking over the room.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Mixed-metal finishes</strong><p>The matchy-matchy bathroom is over. The 2026 look mixes brushed brass taps with matte black hardware and chrome details. We help you pick the right combo at the survey so the result looks planned, not random.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Floating vanities</strong><p>Wall-hung vanities open up the floor space and make cleaning quick. Best in smaller second bathrooms and en suites where space is tight. The fit needs wall blocking at first fix. Retrofit later will likely fail.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Underfloor heating as standard</strong><p>No longer a luxury. Electric underfloor heating is now the norm in top Liverpool bathrooms. The extra cost is small. The comfort lift is huge. We fit it as default on every job above £8,500.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Calm spa look</strong><p>The 2026 design pull is calmer than recent years. Soft lighting. Natural stone and wood. Somewhere to sit. We design around this when clients want a room to switch off in.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>Trends we steer clients away from</h3>
        <p>Not every 2026 trend is worth the money. We steer clients away from bold colour fixtures that date fast. Heavy themed mosaic walls also date quickly. Tech-heavy smart mirrors get out of date long before the bathroom does. We tell you straight at the free survey.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PRICING -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Bathroom Installation Prices Liverpool</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Premium spec at fixed prices. The price covers the bathroom suite, tiles, taps and every brand on this page. We can also quote for labour only if you buy the kit yourself.</p>

      <div class="pf-pricing-grid">

        <div class="pf-price-card pf-price-card-featured">
          <div class="pf-price-badge">MOST POPULAR</div>
          <div class="pf-price-tier">FULL BATHROOM</div>
          <div class="pf-price-name">Complete Design and Installation</div>
          <div class="pf-price-sub">Full strip-out, premium spec, all trades in-house</div>
          <div class="pf-price-amount" style="font-size:2.5rem;">£8,500<small style="font-size:1rem;color:var(--muted);"> supply & fit</small></div>
          <ul class="pf-price-list">
